    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{49}{72}$ of the course.",
      "worked": "The lowest common multiple of $9$ and $8$ is $72$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{9}+\\frac{1}{8}&=\\frac{40}{72}+\\frac{9}{72}\\\\\\frac{5}{9}+\\frac{1}{8}&=\\frac{49}{72}\\end{align*}$$\nHe has covered $\\frac{49}{72}$ of the course.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
